    "answer": {
      "short": "For consecutive integers $n-1,n,n+1$, $(n-1)(n+1)-n^2=n^2-1-n^2=-1$.",
      "worked": "Let the three consecutive integers be $n-1$, $n$ and $n+1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(n-1)(n+1)-n^2&=n^2-1-n^2\\\\&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nThus the result holds for any three consecutive integers.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
